COMMAND: printf 'pid=%s\n' "$$"; readlink "/proc/$$/exe"
EXIT: 1
OUTPUT:
pid=2

INTERPRETATION:
The audit runner's PID namespace reports PID 2 while /proc/2/exe is absent.
Lean uses /proc/<pid>/exe to locate its installation, causing its initial
path-detection failure. The narrowly scoped shim recorded in
01_proc_self_shim.c redirects only those numeric /proc PID executable reads
to /proc/self/exe.

COMMAND: gcc -shared -fPIC -O2 -Wall -Wextra -o /tmp/audit-work/proc_self_shim.so /tmp/audit-work/proc_self_shim.c -ldl; LD_PRELOAD=/tmp/audit-work/proc_self_shim.so lean --version; LD_PRELOAD=/tmp/audit-work/proc_self_shim.so lake --version
EXIT: 0
